log_course_slider&#038;utm_campaign=SEO\"\n                                   class=\"btn btn-outline-secondary btn-sm\">\n                                    Learn More\n                                <\/a>\n                            <\/div>\n                        <\/div>\n                    <\/div>\n\n                \n                    \n                    <div class=\"course-card card-r rounded-4\">\n\n                        <!-- \u2705 SINGLE MEDIA DIV (FIXED) -->\n                        <div class=\"course-media\"\n                             data-lottie=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/uploads\/images\/courses\/json-images\/SEO_json.json\"\n                             data-fallback=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/themes\/newwscube\/assets\/imges\/Image.png\">\n                        <\/div>\n\n                        <div class=\"card-body\">\n                            <h5>SEO Specialist Bootcamp<\/h5>\n\n                            <p class=\"rating\">\n                                4.9 \u2605\u2605\u2605\u2605\u2605\n                                (6983)\n                            <\/p>\n\n                            <ul class=\"course-meta\">\n                                <li>\ud83d\udc64 18000 Learners<\/li>\n                                <li>\u23f1 6 Weeks<\/li>\n                            <\/ul>\n\n                            <div class=\"mt-3\">\n                                                                    <a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/seo-course?utm_source=WsBlog&#038;utm_medium=blog_course_slider&#038;utm_campaign=SEO\"\n                                       target=\"_blank\"\n                                       class=\"btn view-btn btn-sm\">\n                                        View Brochure\n                                    <\/a>\n                                \n                                <a target=\"_blank\"\n                                   href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/seo-course?utm_source=WsBlog&#038;utm_medium=blog_course_slider&#038;utm_campaign=SEO\"\n                                   class=\"btn btn-outline-secondary btn-sm\">\n                                    Learn More\n                                <\/a>\n                            <\/div>\n                        <\/div>\n                    <\/div>\n\n                \n            <\/div>\n        <\/div>\n    <\/section>\n\n    \n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Top 10 Search Engines in the World<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p>Let\u2019s discuss in detail the 10 best search engines:<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">1. Google<\/h3>\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-image\">\n<figure class=\"aligncenter size-full is-resized\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"2432\" height=\"1216\" src=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/12\/google-logo.webp\" alt=\"Google\" class=\"wp-image-17966\" style=\"width:556px;height:auto\" srcset=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/12\/google-logo.webp 2432w, https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/12\/google-logo-300x150.webp 300w, https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/12\/google-logo-1024x512.webp 1024w, https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/12\/google-logo-768x384.webp 768w, https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/12\/google-logo-1536x768.webp 1536w, https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/12\/google-logo-2048x1024.webp 2048w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 2432px) 100vw, 2432px\" \/><\/figure>\n<\/div>\n\n\n<p><a href=\"https:\/\/www.google.com\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener nofollow\">Google<\/a> is the most widely used search engine in the world and has dominated the global search market for many years. Launched in 1998, Google is known for its highly advanced algorithms that focus on relevance, quality, and user intent. It operates globally and supports hundreds of languages, making it the default search choice for most internet users.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>Google\u2019s key strength lies in its ability to understand complex queries and deliver accurate results across web pages, images, videos, news, maps, and shopping. It continuously updates its ranking systems to fight spam and reward high-quality content. Google is also deeply integrated with products like Gmail, YouTube, Google Maps, and Android, which further strengthen its ecosystem.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Best for:<\/h4>\n\n\n\n<p>General web searches, research, local search, business discovery, and up-to-date information.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Key Highlights:<\/h4>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>World\u2019s most popular search engine<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Advanced ranking algorithms<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Strong local and mobile search support<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Integrates with many Google services<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Best overall accuracy and relevance<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">2. Bing<\/h3>\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-image\">\n<figure class=\"aligncenter size-full is-resized\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1200\" height=\"627\" src=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/12\/bing.webp\" alt=\"Bing\" class=\"wp-image-17967\" style=\"aspect-ratio:1.9139164797607604;width:498px;height:auto\" srcset=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/12\/bing.webp 1200w, https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/12\/bing-300x157.webp 300w, https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/12\/bing-1024x535.webp 1024w, https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/12\/bing-768x401.webp 768w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1200px\" \/><\/figure>\n<\/div>\n\n\n<p><a href=\"https:\/\/www.bing.com\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener nofollow\">Bing<\/a> is Microsoft\u2019s search engine and the second most used search engine globally. It powers searches across Microsoft products such as Windows, the Edge browser, and Cortana. Bing has a strong presence in countries like the United States and is widely used as the default search engine on Windows devices.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>Bing focuses heavily on visual search, offering rich image previews, video carousels, and clean layouts. It is also the backbone of Yahoo Search. In recent years, Bing has gained attention for integrating AI-powered features that enhance search experiences.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>For marketers, Bing is valuable because it reaches a slightly different demographic, often including desktop-heavy and enterprise users.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Best for:<\/h4>\n\n\n\n<p>Desktop users, image and video search, Microsoft ecosystem users, and alternative <a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/what-is-seo\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">SEO<\/a> targeting.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Key Highlights:<\/h4>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Powered by Microsoft<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Default on Windows and Edge<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Strong visual search features<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Lower competition for advertisers<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>AI-enhanced search experience<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">3. Yahoo<\/h3>\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-image\">\n<figure class=\"aligncenter size-full is-resized\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"300\" height=\"168\" src=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/12\/yahoo.webp\" alt=\"Yahoo\" class=\"wp-image-17968\" style=\"width:394px;height:auto\"\/><\/figure>\n<\/div>\n\n\n<p><a href=\"https:\/\/www.yahoo.com\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener nofollow\">Yahoo<\/a> is one of the oldest names in the search industry and originally started as a web directory before becoming a full-fledged search engine and content portal. Today, Yahoo Search is powered by Bing\u2019s search technology but maintains its own interface and ecosystem.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>Yahoo is popular for combining search with content such as news, finance, sports, and email services. Many users visit Yahoo not just to search the web, but also to consume daily news and updates. While it no longer leads in search innovation, Yahoo remains relevant due to brand loyalty and its all-in-one portal approach.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Best for:<\/h4>\n\n\n\n<p>Users who prefer news, finance, sports, and email integrated with search.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Key Highlights:<\/h4>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>One of the oldest search brands<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Powered by Bing search results<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Strong content ecosystem (news, finance)<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Popular among long-time users<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Combines portal + search experience<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">4. DuckDuckGo<\/h3>\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-image\">\n<figure class=\"aligncenter size-full is-resized\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"300\" height=\"168\" src=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/12\/duck-duck-go.webp\" alt=\"DuckDuck Go\" class=\"wp-image-17969\" style=\"width:422px;height:auto\"\/><\/figure>\n<\/div>\n\n\n<p><a href=\"https:\/\/duckduckgo.com\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener nofollow\">DuckDuckGo<\/a> is a privacy-focused search engine designed for users who do not want their searches tracked or personalized. Unlike Google and Bing, DuckDuckGo does not store personal data, search history, or user profiles.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>It delivers search results by combining data from multiple sources, including its own crawler and other search providers. DuckDuckGo has grown rapidly among users concerned about data privacy, tracking, and targeted advertising. It also offers browser extensions and a privacy-focused mobile browser.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Best for:<\/h4>\n\n\n\n<p>Privacy-conscious users, anonymous searching, and avoiding personalized results.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Key Highlights:<\/h4>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>No tracking or data collection<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Clean and simple interface<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Same results for all users<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Popular among privacy-first users<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Growing global adoption<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">5. Baidu<\/h3>\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-image\">\n<figure class=\"aligncenter size-full is-resized\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1000\" height=\"600\" src=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/12\/baidu.webp\" alt=\"Baidu\" class=\"wp-image-17970\" style=\"aspect-ratio:1.6666820852028308;width:451px;height:auto\" srcset=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/12\/baidu.webp 1000w, https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/12\/baidu-300x180.webp 300w, https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/12\/baidu-768x461.webp 768w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1000px) 100vw, 1000px\" \/><\/figure>\n<\/div>\n\n\n<p><a href=\"https:\/\/www.baidu.com\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener nofollow\">Baidu<\/a> is the leading search engine in China and dominates the Chinese search market. Due to government regulations and restrictions, Google is not widely accessible in China, which makes Baidu the primary search platform for Chinese users.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>Baidu is heavily optimized for Chinese-language searches and integrates deeply with local services such as maps, music, forums, and cloud products. Its algorithm prioritizes local content and Chinese websites, making it essential for businesses targeting the Chinese market.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Best for:<\/h4>\n\n\n\n<p>Searching content in China and reaching Chinese-speaking audiences.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Key Highlights:<\/h4>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Market leader in China<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Optimized for the Chinese language<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Strong local service integration<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Essential for China-focused SEO<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Operates under regional regulations<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">6. Yandex<\/h3>\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-image\">\n<figure class=\"aligncenter size-full is-resized\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"788\" height=\"443\" src=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/12\/yandex.webp\" alt=\"Yandex\" class=\"wp-image-17971\" style=\"width:408px;height:auto\" srcset=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/12\/yandex.webp 788w, https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/12\/yandex-300x169.webp 300w, https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/12\/yandex-768x432.webp 768w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 788px) 100vw, 788px\" \/><\/figure>\n<\/div>\n\n\n<p><a href=\"https:\/\/yandex.com\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener nofollow\">Yandex<\/a> is the most popular search engine in Russia and several neighboring countries. It was launched in the late 1990s and is often referred to as the \u201cGoogle of Russia.\u201d Yandex is designed specifically to understand the Russian language and its complex grammar, which gives it an advantage over global search engines in that region.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>Beyond web search, Yandex offers a wide ecosystem of services, including maps, email, cloud storage, ride-hailing, and music streaming. Its search algorithm is highly localized, focusing on regional intent, local businesses, and language nuances.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>For businesses and content creators targeting Russia or Eastern Europe, Yandex plays a critical role in visibility and traffic generation.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Best for:<\/h4>\n\n\n\n<p>Users searching in the Russian language, regional content discovery, and businesses targeting Eastern Europe.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Key Highlights:<\/h4>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Dominant search engine in Russia<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Strong language and regional understanding<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Wide ecosystem beyond search<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/local-seo\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Local SEO<\/a> importance in Eastern Europe<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Optimized for Cyrillic content<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">7. Brave Search<\/h3>\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-image\">\n<figure class=\"aligncenter size-full\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"406\" height=\"124\" src=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/12\/brave-search.webp\" alt=\"Brave Search\" class=\"wp-image-17972\" srcset=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/12\/brave-search.webp 406w, https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/12\/brave-search-300x92.webp 300w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 406px) 100vw, 406px\" \/><\/figure>\n<\/div>\n\n\n<p><a href=\"https:\/\/search.brave.com\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener nofollow\">Brave Search<\/a> is a relatively new but fast-growing search engine built by the creators of the Brave browser. Unlike many alternatives, Brave Search uses its own independent index, reducing reliance on Google or Bing. This makes it a truly independent search engine in terms of infrastructure.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>Brave Search focuses heavily on user privacy, transparency, and unbiased results. It does not track users, store personal data, or create search profiles. The platform is closely integrated with the Brave browser, but it can also be used independently. Brave Search appeals strongly to users who want privacy without sacrificing result quality.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Best for:<\/h4>\n\n\n\n<p>Privacy-focused users are looking for an independent alternative to Google.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Key Highlights:<\/h4>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Uses its own search index<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>No tracking or user profiling<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Integrated with the Brave browser<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Transparent ranking approach<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Growing adoption among tech users<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">8. Ecosia<\/h3>\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-image\">\n<figure class=\"aligncenter size-full is-resized\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1378\" height=\"1378\" src=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/12\/ecosia.webp\" alt=\"Ecosia\" class=\"wp-image-17973\" style=\"width:366px;height:auto\" srcset=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/12\/ecosia.webp 1378w, https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/12\/ecosia-300x300.webp 300w, https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/12\/ecosia-1024x1024.webp 1024w, https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/12\/ecosia-150x150.webp 150w, https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/12\/ecosia-768x768.webp 768w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1378px) 100vw, 1378px\" \/><\/figure>\n<\/div>\n\n\n<p><a href=\"https:\/\/www.ecosia.org\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener nofollow\">Ecosia<\/a> is a unique search engine that uses its ad revenue to fund tree-planting projects around the world. Based in Germany, Ecosia partners with Bing for search results while focusing its mission on environmental sustainability.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>Every search contributes to Ecosia\u2019s revenue, which is transparently published in financial reports. The company claims that a certain number of searches lead to planting one tree, making it popular among environmentally conscious users. Ecosia also emphasizes privacy by not selling user data and limiting tracking.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Best for:<\/h4>\n\n\n\n<p>Users who want their searches to contribute to environmental causes.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Key Highlights:<\/h4>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Profits used for tree planting<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Powered by Bing search results<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Strong environmental mission<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Privacy-friendly approach<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Transparent financial reporting<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">9. Startpage<\/h3>\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-image\">\n<figure class=\"aligncenter size-full is-resized\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"324\" height=\"156\" src=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/12\/startpage.webp\" alt=\"Startpage\" class=\"wp-image-17974\" style=\"aspect-ratio:2.077045933686833;width:542px;height:auto\" srcset=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/12\/startpage.webp 324w, https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/12\/startpage-300x144.webp 300w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 324px) 100vw, 324px\" \/><\/figure>\n<\/div>\n\n\n<p><a href=\"https:\/\/www.startpage.com\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener nofollow\">Startpage<\/a> is a privacy-focused search engine that delivers Google search results without tracking users. It acts as a privacy layer between the user and Google, ensuring searches remain anonymous.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>Unlike many search engines, Startpage does not store IP addresses, search history, or personal identifiers. This makes it appealing to users who trust Google\u2019s result quality but dislike data collection. Startpage is especially useful for users who want accurate results without personalization or tracking influence.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Best for:<\/h4>\n\n\n\n<p>Users who want Google-quality results with complete privacy.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Key Highlights:<\/h4>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Uses Google results anonymously<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>No tracking or data storage<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Clean, simple interface<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Ideal for privacy-conscious professionals<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Strong trust among security-focused users<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">10. Ask.com<\/h3>\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-image\">\n<figure class=\"aligncenter size-full is-resized\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"300\" height=\"168\" src=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/12\/ask-com.webp\" alt=\"Ask.com\" class=\"wp-image-17975\" style=\"width:432px;height:auto\"\/><\/figure>\n<\/div>\n\n\n<p><a href=\"https:\/\/www.ask.com\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener nofollow\">Ask.com<\/a> started as a question-and-answer\u2013based search engine, originally known as Ask Jeeves. Its focus was on allowing users to search in natural language questions rather than keywords.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>Today, Ask.com operates more as a content-driven search platform, providing curated answers, articles, and FAQs. While it no longer competes directly with Google or Bing in raw search scale, it still attracts users looking for straightforward answers and topic-based browsing.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Best for:<\/h4>\n\n\n\n<p>Simple question-based searches and informational browsing.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Key Highlights:<\/h4>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Question-focused search format<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Easy for beginners<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Content and answer-driven results<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Long-standing search brand<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Simpler alternative to major engines<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n        <div class=\"container position-relative mb-2\">\n            <div class=\"row pb-4\">\n                <h2 style=\"font-size:32px\">Upcoming Masterclass<\/h2>\n              